          "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we sketch a construction of a deformation theory for the\nstack of coherent sheaves for any algebraic space <MATH_0001> over a ring <MATH_0002>.\nThis material is obsolete due to the improved discussion in\nQuot, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nOur setup will be the following. We assume given\n<STRUCT_0004>\n<STRUCT_0005> a ring <MATH_0003>,\n<STRUCT_0006> an algebraic space <MATH_0004> over <MATH_0005>,\n<STRUCT_0007> a <MATH_0006>-algebra <MATH_0007>, set\n<MATH_0008>, and\n<STRUCT_0008> a finitely presented <MATH_0009>-module <MATH_0010>\nflat over <MATH_0011>.\n<STRUCT_0009>\nIn this situation we will consider all possible surjections\n<MATH_0012>\nwhere <MATH_0013> is a <MATH_0014>-algebra whose kernel <MATH_0015> is an ideal of square zero\nin <MATH_0016>. Given <MATH_0017> we obtain a first order thickening <MATH_0018>\nof algebraic spaces over <MATH_0019>. For each of these we consider\nthe problem of lifting <MATH_0020> to a finitely presented module\n<MATH_0021> on <MATH_0022> flat over <MATH_0023>. We would like to replicate the\nresults of Deformation Theory, Lemma <REF_0002>\nin this setting.\n\n<STRUCT_0010><STRUCT_0011>\nTo be more precise let <MATH_0024> denote the category\nof pairs <MATH_0025> where <MATH_0026> is a\nfinitely presented module on <MATH_0027> flat over <MATH_0028> and\n<MATH_0029> is an isomorphism.\nMorphisms <MATH_0030>\nare isomorphisms <MATH_0031> which are compatible\nwith <MATH_0032> and <MATH_0033>.\nThe set of isomorphism classes of <MATH_0034>\nis denoted <MATH_0035>.\n\n<STRUCT_0012><STRUCT_0013>\nLet <MATH_0036> be a sheaf of <MATH_0037>-modules\non <MATH_0038> flat over <MATH_0039>. We introduce the category\n<MATH_0040> of pairs\n<MATH_0041> where <MATH_0042> is a sheaf of\n<MATH_0043>-modules flat over <MATH_0044> and <MATH_0045>\nis an isomorphism <MATH_0046>.\n\n",
